## 🔑 Key Concepts Emphasized

### 1. Vectorization
- R's greatest strength
- Operations apply to entire vectors instantly
- 100-1000x faster than loops
- **Key Insight**: Always prefer vectorization over loops

### 2. 1-Based Indexing
- First element at position 1 (not 0 like Python)
- Consistent throughout R
- Common source of bugs when switching languages
- **Key Insight**: Remember x[1] is first element

### 3. Type Hierarchy
- logical < integer < double < character
- Automatic coercion to highest type
- Preserves information
- **Key Insight**: Mixing types converts all to highest

### 4. Data Frames
- Like spreadsheets/databases
- Most used structure in data analysis
- Each column can be different type
- **Key Insight**: df$name returns vector, df[name] returns data frame

### 5. Functions as Objects
- Can be assigned to variables
- Can be passed as arguments
- Closures remember environment
- **Key Insight**: Functions are first-class objects

