**Why Loops Are Usually Not Recommended:**

```r
# SLOW: Loop approach
result <- numeric(0)
for (i in 1:1000000) {
  result <- c(result, i^2)
}

# FAST: Vectorized approach
result <- (1:1000000)^2

# Use apply family instead of loops
lapply(list, function(x) x^2)  # Better than loop

# Most R operations are vectorized internally
# Loops slow down due to interpretation overhead
```

