### Q8: Explain recycling in R vectors

**A:**
**Recycling** means R repeats shorter vectors automatically to match length:

```r
# Basic recycling
c(1, 2, 3) + c(10, 20)
# R repeats c(10, 20) to c(10, 20, 10)
# Result: c(11, 22, 13) ⚠️ Might be unexpected!

# Useful recycling
c(1, 2, 3, 4) * 2  # Recycles 2 to c(2, 2, 2, 2)
# Result: c(2, 4, 6, 8) ✓

# Dangerous recycling
df <- data.frame(x = 1:10, y = 1:3)
# ⚠️ y gets recycled: c(1, 2, 3, 1, 2, 3, 1, 2, 3, 1)
# Usually not what you want!

# Explicit recycling (safer)
