## ⚡ Common Pitfalls & Solutions

### 1. 1-Based Indexing
```r
# Python: x[0] = first element
# R: x[1] = first element
x <- c("a", "b", "c")
x[1]  # "a" (not x[0]!)
```

### 2. Recycling
```r
c(1, 2) + c(10, 20, 30)
# Silently recycles shorter vector!
# c(1,2,1) + c(10,20,30) = c(11, 22, 31)
# ⚠️ Often a bug!
```

### 3. Type Coercion
```r
c(1, "2")  # Becomes c("1", "2")
# Numeric becomes character!
```

### 4. Data Frame Access
```r
df$name       # Vector
df["name"]    # Data frame!
df[["name"]]  # Vector
# Different return types!
```

### 5. Factor Gotcha
```r
f <- factor(c("1", "2", "3"))
as.numeric(f)  # c(1, 2, 3) - wrong!
as.numeric(as.character(f))  # Correct
```

### 6. Infinite Loops
```r
while (i <= 5) {
  print(i)
  # Forgot: i <- i + 1
}  # ⚠️ Infinite loop!
```

### 7. NA Propagation
```r
5 + NA  # NA (unknown + known = unknown)
