## 🏗️ Data Type Hierarchy

```
Every operation follows this hierarchy for type coercion:

┌─────────┐
│ logical │  (TRUE, FALSE)
└────┬────┘
     │ (if mixed with below, converts up)
     ↓
┌─────────┐
│ integer │  (1L, 2L, 3L)
└────┬────┘
     │
     ↓
┌─────────┐
│ double  │  (1.5, 2.0, 3.14)
└────┬────┘
     │
     ↓
┌──────────┐
│character │  ("hello", "world")
└──────────┘

Example: c(TRUE, "hello") → c("TRUE", "hello")
         (logical becomes character)
```

