## 🔑 R's Key Characteristics

| Feature | What It Means | Example |
|---------|--------------|---------|
| **1-Indexed** | First element at position 1, not 0 | `x[1]` = first element |
| **Vectorized** | Operations apply to all elements | `c(1,2)*2` = `c(2,4)` |
| **Homogeneous Vectors** | All elements same type | `c(1, "2")` → `c("1", "2")` |
| **Heterogeneous Lists** | Different types mixed | `list(name="John", age=25)` |
| **Type Coercion** | Automatic conversion to higher type | `c(1, 3.14)` → `c(1, 3.14)` (integer→double) |

