## 🧬 Type Coercion Sequence

```
When mixing types, R converts following this path:

Input: c(TRUE, 1, 1.5, "text")
       (logical, integer, double, character)

Step 1: Mix logical + integer
       c(TRUE, 1) → c(1, 1) [logical→integer]
       Now: c(1, 1, 1.5, "text")

Step 2: Mix integer + double
       c(1, 1) + 1.5 → c(1.0, 1.0) [integer→double]
       Now: c(1.0, 1.0, 1.5, "text")

Step 3: Mix double + character
       c(1.0, 1.0, 1.5) + "text" → [double→character]
       Now: c("1", "1", "1.5", "text")

FINAL: c("1", "1", "1.5", "text")  [All character]

RULE: Converts to highest type in hierarchy to preserve info
```

