## 🚀 Performance Comparison

```
OPERATION: Create vector of 1 million squares

VECTORIZED (FASTEST):
result <- (1:1e6)^2
┌────────────────────────────┐
│ Time: ~1 ms (instant)      │
│ Method: Single C operation │
└────────────────────────────┘

sapply (FAST):
result <- sapply(1:1e6, function(x) x^2)
┌────────────────────────────┐
│ Time: ~50 ms               │
│ Method: apply family (C)   │
└────────────────────────────┘

LOOP WITH PRE-ALLOCATION (SLOW):
result <- numeric(1e6)
for (i in 1:1e6) result[i] <- i^2
┌────────────────────────────┐
│ Time: ~2 seconds           │
│ Method: Interpreted loop   │
└────────────────────────────┘

LOOP WITHOUT PRE-ALLOCATION (VERY SLOW):
result <- numeric(0)
for (i in 1:1e6) result <- c(result, i^2)
┌────────────────────────────┐
│ Time: ~30 seconds!         │
│ Method: Interpreted + grows│
└────────────────────────────┘

RATIO: Vectorized is 2000x-30000x faster!
```

